==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tights Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Loincloth Cat''' when obtained from the [[Skirt Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This cat has underwhelming stats outside of the very beginning of the game. Its use is, therefore, not recommended aside from an assortment of [[Cat Combo]]s.

==='''True Form'''===
For the most part, Loincloth Cat is a weaker, budgeted [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs Cat]]. However, it does stand out in [[Cats of the Cosmos]], in stages with the [[Restriction Stage|restriction]] of [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]] only. Loincloth Cat is useful for breaking enemy barriers on those levels with her Barrier Breaker ability, especially against [[General GreGory]] and [[Le'Solar]].

Notably, [[UltraBaaBaa]] (has a Barrier with a massive 266,000 HP) appears in stages with this restriction in Cats of the Cosmos Chapter 2. So, unless you have Li'l Macho Legs Cat, [[Tasmanian Giant Crab (Special Cat)|Tasmanian Giant Crab]] or the Breakerblast Cannon, you should use Loincloth Cat to destroy her Barrier in order to beat these stages.

==='''Talents'''===
Even when fully Talented, despite the massive cost of getting there, this unit still can't compete with other [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs]] variants.

Although its [[Weaken]] against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies Talent seems useful, it is entirely outclassed by [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]], who has higher range, the ability to [[Slow]] Aliens, and his own cheaper Weaken Talent. While this Talent may see some ''rare'' use in [[Restriction Stage]]s such as [[Aguham (Cats of the Cosmos)|Aguham]] and [[Wrath of the Wormhole (Merciless)|Wrath of the Wormhole]], buying such an expensive Talent for one or two stages is generally ill-advised.

==='''Orb'''===
The best orb for it would be a Defense UP against aliens, although Skirt Cat is not worth spending any talent orbs on.

